<title>LITHUANIA: Yields edge up on 91-day Lithuanian T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yields edge up on 91-day Lithuanian T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields edged up on 91-day Lithuanian Treasury bills and all of the 50 million litas issue was sold, the country's central bank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The average yield was 9.37 percent, up from the 9.19 percent offered at the last auction for 91-day paper on May 12.</p>
<p>The settlement date is May 22 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>August 21.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MATURITY MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD  LAST AV. YIELD</p>
<p> 50   66.365  91-Days  9.03/9.70	  9.37	   9.19</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
